(40371, 214, 347, '<td valign="top">OK, another rose. The background is a little busy, I think, and the lighting a little hard-edged for a soft subject -- perhaps try lighting by reflection or putting white (or red) fabric in front of the sun. That might also help the orange tinge on the rose.</td>', 'OK, another rose. The background is a little busy, I think, and the lighting a little hard-edged for a soft subject -- perhaps try lighting by reflection or putting white (or red) fabric in front of the sun. That might also help the orange tinge on the rose.', '2002-03-11 19:08:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(40372, 214, 27, '<td valign="top">The color is too faded.</td>', 'The color is too faded.', '2002-03-11 00:40:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(40373, 214, 203, '<td valign="top">Very nice photo.  The reason for the low mark is to me it is cliche and does not even seem like a red cliche.</td>', 'Very nice photo.  The reason for the low mark is to me it is cliche and does not even seem like a red cliche.', '2002-03-11 00:52:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(40374, 214, 352, '<td valign="top">I find the background to be rather distracting.  Almost to the point of taking all my attention away from the central subject.</td>', 'I find the background to be rather distracting.  Almost to the point of taking all my attention away from the central subject.', '2002-03-11 00:56:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(40375, 214, 496, '<td valign="top">perspective not that interesting.</td>', 'perspective not that interesting.', '2002-03-11 02:43:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(40376, 214, 283, '<td valign="top">Your rose has really good definition and the angle of the shot is pleasing. The only thing I can think of changing is maybe the color of the red. Make the red a little darker and a little red''er. I think you might be able to use levels on photoshop if you have access to it. Maybe an input level of 60/1.68/2.20 (rgb) might help it stand out more. Ok enough blah blah from me :).</td>', 'Your rose has really good definition and the angle of the shot is pleasing. The only thing I can think of changing is maybe the color of the red. Make the red a little darker and a little red''er. I think you might be able to use levels on photoshop if you have access to it. Maybe an input level of 60/1.68/2.20 (rgb) might help it stand out more. Ok enough blah blah from me :).', '2002-03-11 07:10:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(40377, 214, 459, '<td valign="top">Nice lighting. Color is not red.</td>', 'Nice lighting. Color is not red.', '2002-03-11 12:59:00.000000', NULL, 1),
